---
import Journey from '../../layouts/Journey.astro';
import Step from '../../components/journey/Step.astro';
import Next from '../../components/journey/Next.astro';
import More from '../../components/journey/More.astro';
import ForLevel from '../../components/level/ForLevel.astro';
import CopyPrompt from '../../components/site/CopyPrompt.astro';
import Fact from '../../components/data/Fact.astro';
import Verified from '../../components/data/Verified.astro';
import LessonRef from '../../components/journey/LessonRef.astro';
import Term from '../../components/journey/Term.astro';
---
<Journey chapter="parallel" first="three" title="Side by side" description="Several helpers can work at once if each has its own copy of the project. Their finished work is merged into main one piece at a time.">
  <Step id="three" title="Three at once, one folder">
    <p>Three <Term id="helper">helpers</Term> from <LessonRef id="handoff" />, each with its own task, all editing the same folder. Orange tiles are edits that landed on top of another helper’s.</p>
  </Step>
  <Step id="copies" title="Give each its own copy">
    <p>Each helper gets its own copy of the project on its own <Term id="branch" />: a <Term id="worktree" />, the small plate beside it. Finished work merges into <Term id="main" /> one piece at a time.</p>
    <div class="pick">
      <button type="button" data-do="own" data-val="own" data-default aria-pressed="true">A copy each</button>
      <button type="button" data-do="own" data-val="shared" aria-pressed="false">One shared folder</button>
    </div>
    <More title="How to set it up" level="technical">
      <ForLevel is="plain">
        <CopyPrompt compact title="Ask for parallel work">{`Do these three tasks in parallel, each in its own git worktree on its own branch:\n1. Sort members by rating.\n2. Add a search box.\n3. Export the list to CSV.\nWhen one is finished and its tests pass, merge it into main, then the next.`}</CopyPrompt>
      </ForLevel>
      <ForLevel is="technical engineer">
        <pre class="j-code"><code>{`git worktree add ../club-search -b search   # a copy on its own branch
cd ../club-search && claude                 # one agent per copy
git switch main && git merge search          # when its tests pass
git worktree remove ../club-search
git branch -d search                          # the branch outlives the copy`}</code></pre>
      </ForLevel>
      <ForLevel is="engineer">
        <p>Where it breaks: one branch can be checked out in one worktree only; each copy needs its own install and its own dev-server port; two copies that touch the same file still conflict at the merge, so split tasks by file.</p>
      </ForLevel>
      <p><Fact id="harnesses.claudeCode.features" show="claim" /></p>
      <p><Fact id="harnesses.claudeCode.subagentWorktree" show="claim" /></p>
    </More>
  </Step>
  <Step id="more" title="How many?">
    <p>More helpers finish sooner, and every report lands in the agent’s window. Watch its number climb.</p>
    <div class="controls">
      <label class="control"><span>Helpers <output>5</output></span>
        <input type="range" min="1" max="5" step="1" value="5" data-bind="n" aria-label="How many helpers" />
      </label>
    </div>
    <ForLevel is="engineer"><p>Copies stop clashes on disk, not in the code: two branches that change the same function still conflict at merge. Split tasks by the files they own.</p></ForLevel>
    <Next from="parallel" />
  </Step>
  <Fragment slot="foot">
    <p>The tasks, the clashes and the window numbers are made up; which tasks clash is fixed, so a run reads the same each time.</p>
    <Verified ids={['harnesses.claudeCode.features', 'harnesses.claudeCode.subagentWorktree']} />
  </Fragment>
</Journey>
